{"id": "EUVD-2026-108182", "enisaUuid": "6b208c59-5c50-3bf4-b378-ef5104197335", "description": "In EmberZNet 9.1.1 and earlier, a malformed Publish Billing Period command can result in a recursive function call that will never reach its end condition. These messages must come from a device that has already joined the network. Only devices supporting the Price Cluster are impacted.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T13:44:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T10:56:09", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/SiliconLabsSoftware/docs-security-advisories/blob/main/Advisories/500-599/A-00000590.md"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pmf2-p6v3-p6jr", "CVE-2026-66282"], "assigner": "Silabs", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4c4daa95-9b48-3199-a2f2-a056a40676c5", "product": {"name": "EmberZNet", "vendor": {"name": "silabs.com"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.1.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4c68ce21-31ee-37d6-b9e0-920fed84bdf9", "vendor": {"name": "Silicon Labs"}}], "isExploited": false}